+++ /dev/null
@@ -1,159 +0,0 @@
-[PATCH 3/3] build_eebbk_clang11.sh: build techpack/audio INTO the kernel (TECHPACK=y)
-
-*** THIS IS THE ACTUAL SOUND FIX ***
-
-An earlier revision of this script passed TECHPACK=n, on the theory that the
-device loads the whole QCOM audio stack as vendor DLKM modules from
-/vendor/lib/modules and that building it in would collide with them.  That
-theory was wrong, and it is precisely what produced a completely silent
-device:
-
-  * techpack/Kbuild reads   obj-${TECHPACK} += stub/ audio/ data/
-    so TECHPACK=n compiles ONLY techpack/stub/.  Measured on the real build:
-    the whole image contained exactly ONE techpack object, an empty
-    techpack/built-in.o -- zero audio code and, critically, no ADSP loader.
-
-  * techpack/audio/dsp/adsp-loader.c (CONFIG_MSM_ADSP_LOADER=y, set by
-    techpack/audio/config/sm6150auto.conf) is what binds the
-    "qcom,adsp-loader" device tree node and calls subsystem_get("adsp") to
-    load adsp.mbn through the qcom,pil-tz-generic node.  Without it the ADSP
-    never comes up, which is exactly what the device reported:
-
-        adsprpcd: apps_dev_init failed for domain 0,
-                  errno Transport endpoint is not connected   (endless loop)
-        audio_hw_utils: audio_extn_utils_open_snd_mixer: retry, retry_num 18
-        /sys/class/sound/  ->  timer          (no card0)
-        ServiceManager: Waiting for service 'media.audio_policy'  -> boot hangs
-
-  * The vendor's own audio_adsp_loader.ko in /vendor/lib/modules cannot take
-    over: it was linked against the vendor kernel and is ABI incompatible
-    with a kernel built from this tree (struct module / symbol CRC mismatch),
-    so it cannot boot the ADSP here.
-
-With TECHPACK=y (techpack/Kbuild's own default -- simply do not pass
-TECHPACK=n) the image carries a self-consistent, ABI-matched audio stack:
-
-    asoc/  sm6150.c machine driver (compatible "qcom,sm6150-asoc-snd",
-           card name taken from the DT qcom,model -- on this device the BBK
-           overlay sets "sm6150-wcd9375-snd-card"),
-           bolero / wsa-macro / va-macro / rx-macro / tx-macro,
-           wcd937x + wcd937x-slave, wcd_mbhc, aw882xx smart-PA
-    dsp/   q6afe/q6asm/q6adm/q6core, APR, SSR, and adsp-loader.c
-    ipc/   apr / glink transports
-
-The device tree already describes all of it and is left untouched: the
-factory DTB in boot.img is preserved byte for byte and the bootloader still
-applies the factory dtbo, so the sound node
-(compatible "qcom,sm6150-asoc-snd", qcom,model "sm6150-wcd9375-snd-card")
-matches this machine driver exactly.
-
-Also in this script:
-  * LD=ld.lld -- GNU ld 2.38 cannot link this 4.14 tree (see the camera
-    folder's vmlinux.lds.S patch).
-  * KBUILD_BUILD_USER=cp / KBUILD_BUILD_HOST=ubuntu165 -- same as factory.
-  * CONFIG_MODULE_SIG_FORCE=n in the generated .config.
-And required outside it:
-  * an empty .scmversion in the source root, otherwise a tree containing .git
-    makes kernelrelease "4.14.190-perf+" and every vendor module is rejected
-    on vermagic.
-diff --git a/build_eebbk_clang11.sh b/build_eebbk_clang11.sh
-new file mode 100755
-index 0000000..57994d3
---- /dev/null
-+++ b/build_eebbk_clang11.sh
-@@ -0,0 +1,95 @@
-+#!/bin/bash
-+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-+# EEBBK S6 (P20H130 / sm6150 / sdmmagpiep) kernel build script
-+#
-+#   clang 11 + LLVM lld, Android 10/11 CAF msm-4.14 kernel
-+#
-+# Key points
-+#   1. techpack/audio MUST be built into the kernel image (TECHPACK=y, which is
-+#      also techpack/Kbuild's own default -- do NOT pass TECHPACK=n).
-+#      This is what fixes "no sound":
-+#        * the image then carries the whole QCOM audio stack (Q6/APR, bolero,
-+#          wcd937x, wsa-macro, aw882xx smart-PA, the sm6150 machine driver);
-+#        * and, above all, CONFIG_MSM_ADSP_LOADER=y, i.e. techpack/audio/dsp/
-+#          adsp-loader.c, which binds the "qcom,adsp-loader" DT node and calls
-+#          subsystem_get("adsp") to bring the ADSP up.  Without it the ADSP
-+#          never boots, adsprpcd loops on "Transport endpoint is not
-+#          connected", audioserver never publishes media.audio_policy and the
-+#          device freezes on the boot animation.
-+#      The vendor copy of that loader in /vendor/lib/modules cannot do the job
-+#      here: those modules were built against a different kernel and are ABI
-+#      incompatible with this tree.
-+#   2. The link must use ld.lld: the aarch64 GNU ld shipped with modern
-+#      distributions (2.38) mis-places the .bss.rtic section and fails with
-+#      "relocation truncated to fit: R_AARCH64_ADR_PREL_PG_HI21".
-+#
-+# Usage:
-+#   ./build_eebbk_clang11.sh                      # factory config + TECHPACK=y
-+#   TECHPACK_MODE=n ./build_eebbk_clang11.sh      # old, sound-less build
-+#   CONFIG=h130.config ./build_eebbk_clang11.sh   # build with the repo config
-+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-+set -e
-+
-+TAG=${TAG:-eebbk}
-+OUT=${OUT:-out}
-+JOBS=${JOBS:-$(nproc)}
-+TECHPACK_MODE=${TECHPACK_MODE:-y}
-+CCBIN=${CCBIN:-clang-11}
-+LDBIN=${LDBIN:-ld.lld}
-+KCONFIG=${CONFIG:-h130_factory.config}
-+
-+cd "$(dirname "$0")"
-+
-+export ARCH=arm64
-+export SUBARCH=arm64
-+export CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-linux-gnu-
-+export CLANG_TRIPLE=aarch64-linux-gnu-
-+export TARGET_PRODUCT=sm6150
-+export KBUILD_BUILD_USER=${KBUILD_BUILD_USER:-cp}
-+export KBUILD_BUILD_HOST=${KBUILD_BUILD_HOST:-ubuntu165}
-+
-+echo "== toolchain =="
-+$CCBIN --version | head -1
-+$LDBIN --version | head -1
-+
-+# techpack/Kbuild contains "TECHPACK?=y", so leaving this unset also builds the
-+# audio stack in.  Only an explicit TECHPACK=n removes it (and with it the ADSP
-+# loader -> no sound at all).
-+echo "== configure ($KCONFIG, TECHPACK=$TECHPACK_MODE) =="
-+rm -rf "$OUT"
-+mkdir -p "$OUT"
-+cp "arch/arm64/configs/$KCONFIG" "$OUT/.config"
-+make -j"$JOBS" O="$OUT" CC="$CCBIN" LD="$LDBIN" TECHPACK="$TECHPACK_MODE" olddefconfig
-+
-+# The vendor DLKM modules in /vendor/lib/modules were signed with the vendor
-+# module key and carry CRCs computed in the complete vendor tree.  A kernel
-+# built here cannot match either, so relax just those two checks - the
-+# vermagic string itself stays identical (that one must match!):
-+#   * CONFIG_MODULE_SIG_FORCE=n   (keep CONFIG_MODULE_SIG / MODVERSIONS =y)
-+#   * kernel/module.c check_version() accepts CRC mismatches (see bad_version)
-+echo "== relax module signature force =="
-+sed -i 's/^CONFIG_MODULE_SIG_FORCE=y/# CONFIG_MODULE_SIG_FORCE is not set/' "$OUT/.config"
-+make -j"$JOBS" O="$OUT" CC="$CCBIN" LD="$LDBIN" TECHPACK="$TECHPACK_MODE" olddefconfig
-+grep -E '^CONFIG_MODVERSIONS|^# CONFIG_MODULE_SIG_FORCE' "$OUT/.config"
-+
-+echo "== build Image.gz =="
-+make -j"$JOBS" O="$OUT" CC="$CCBIN" LD="$LDBIN" TECHPACK="$TECHPACK_MODE" DTC=dtc Image.gz
-+
-+echo "== artifacts =="
-+ls -la "$OUT/arch/arm64/boot/Image.gz" "$OUT/vmlinux"
-+echo "kernel release: $(make -s O=$OUT kernelrelease 2>/dev/null || true)"
-+
-+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-+# Verify the audio stack really made it into the image.  A correct build shows
-+# non-zero counts for all of these; the old TECHPACK=n build showed 0 for the
-+# audio stack and only the camera strings.
-+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-+if [ -f "$OUT/arch/arm64/boot/Image.gz" ]; then
-+  echo "== audio stack inside Image.gz =="
-+  gzip -dc "$OUT/arch/arm64/boot/Image.gz" > /tmp/_img_check
-+  for s in adsp-loader q6afe bolero wcd937x wsa wcd_mbhc aw882xx \
-+           sm6150-wcd9375-snd-card driver/BackCamera_info; do
-+    printf "  %-28s %s\n" "$s" "$(grep -a -c "$s" /tmp/_img_check)"
-+  done
-+  rm -f /tmp/_img_check
-+fi
diff --git a/s6patch声音/0004-sm6150-aw882xx-speaker-codec.patch b/s6patch声音/0004-sm6150-aw882xx-speaker-codec.patch
